# Salivo Stage 36.1 async runtime + Stage 36.2 HTTP transport + Stage 36.3 framework ABI - the single canonical definition.
#
# Consumers (none of them keep a second copy of this table):
#   crates/salivo_semantic   declares every intrinsic from it (include_str!)
#   crates/salivo_backend    maps intrinsic -> C symbol from it (include_str!)
#   compiler/stage3          reads it at compile time (runtimeIntrinsic)
#   scripts/stage36_1.py     verifies the C definitions against it and emits the ABI manifest
#
# Backends: Windows (IOCP + fibers), POSIX (epoll on Linux / poll(2) elsewhere + ucontext fibers).
#
# Every parameter and return value is a 64-bit integer (`int`) or a NUL-terminated UTF-8 pointer
# (`string`). Runtime objects cross the boundary only as opaque generation-tagged handles, so no
# aggregate layout crosses it. Negative `int` results are error codes (see AIO_ERRORS).
#
# Columns: intrinsic|c symbol|return|params|blocking|thread safety|ownership & lifetime
@abi_version 36300
@errors 0:Ok,-1:WouldBlock,-2:Eof,-3:ConnectionReset,-4:Timeout,-5:Cancelled,-6:Closed,-7:InvalidArgument,-8:Os,-9:Shutdown,-10:InvalidHandle,-11:Full,-12:Unsupported,-13:NotInTask,-14:ConnectionRefused,-15:AddressInUse,-16:Truncated,-17:TaskFailed,-18:BadMessage,-19:InvalidHeader,-20:InvalidFraming,-21:HeaderTooLarge,-22:BodyTooLarge,-23:VersionNotSupported,-24:ProtocolError,-25:StreamReset,-26:FlowControl,-27:Compression,-28:Refused,-29:GoingAway
rtaioabiversion|salivo_aio_abi_version|int||never|any thread|none
rtaiocreate|salivo_aio_create|int|int|never|any thread; up to 32 live runtimes|caller owns the runtime handle until rtaiodestroy
rtaiouse|salivo_aio_use|int|int|never|calling OS thread|selects the runtime handle-less calls from this thread use (0 clears); tasks always use their own runtime
rtaiostart|salivo_aio_start|int|int|never|any thread|starts runtime-owned workers, reactor and blocking pool
rtaiorun|salivo_aio_run|int|int,int,int|parks the calling OS thread (never a worker)|non-worker threads|root task owned by the runtime; result via rtaiolastvalue
rtaioshutdown|salivo_aio_shutdown|int|int|never|any thread|cancels every live task; later spawns fail with Shutdown
rtaiojoin|salivo_aio_join|int|int,int|parks the calling OS thread|non-worker threads|joins every runtime-owned OS thread; timeout -1 waits forever
rtaiodestroy|salivo_aio_destroy|int|int|never|any thread after rtaiojoin|frees all runtime-owned objects; the handle becomes invalid
rtaiostat|salivo_aio_stat|int|int,int|never|any thread|read-only counters derived from live runtime state
rtaiolastvalue|salivo_aio_last_value|int||never|task-local (fiber) or thread-local|value produced by the caller's previous successful operation
rtaiolasttext|salivo_aio_last_text_str|string||never|task-local or thread-local|hands the last received text to the caller (once)
rtaiolastpeer|salivo_aio_last_peer_str|string||never|task-local or thread-local|textual address of the last datagram sender; new string owned by the caller
rtaiolastoserror|salivo_aio_last_os_error|int||never|task-local or thread-local|OS error code behind the caller's previous Os error
rtaioworkerid|salivo_aio_worker_id|int||never|any thread|none
rtaiospawn|salivo_aio_spawn|int|int,int|never|any thread|caller owns the task handle; release with rtaiorelease
rtaiospawnowning|salivo_aio_spawn_owning|int|int,int|never|any thread|the task owns the handle passed as its argument: if it is cancelled before its first run the runtime closes/releases that handle; on error the caller keeps it
rtaiospawnon|salivo_aio_spawn_on|int|int,int,int|never|any thread|spawns on an explicit runtime; caller owns the task handle
rtaioawait|salivo_aio_await|int|int|suspends the task; parks a non-worker thread|any thread|borrows the handle; result via rtaiolastvalue
rtaioawaittimeout|salivo_aio_await_timeout|int|int,int|suspends the task; parks a non-worker thread|any thread|borrows the handle; on Timeout the target task is cancelled
rtaiorelease|salivo_aio_release|int|int|never|any thread|consumes the handle; the task is freed once it is also terminal
rtaiocancel|salivo_aio_cancel|int|int|never|any thread|borrows the handle
rtaioiscancelled|salivo_aio_is_cancelled|int|int|never|any thread|0 means the calling task; observing true marks the task Cancelled
rtaiotaskstate|salivo_aio_task_state|int|int|never|any thread|borrows the handle
rtaioyield|salivo_aio_yield|int||suspends the task until rescheduled|task only|none
rtaiosafepoint|salivo_aio_safepoint|int||yields only when the time slice expired|task only|inserted by the compiler at loop back-edges of programs that import salivo.std.runtime
rtaiocurrent|salivo_aio_current|int||never|any thread|returns a borrowed handle of the calling task (0 outside tasks)
rtaiofail|salivo_aio_fail|int|int|never|task only|marks the calling task Failed with the code when it returns
rtaiosleep|salivo_aio_sleep|int|int|suspends the task on a runtime timer; parks a non-worker thread|any thread|timer node lives in the caller frame and is unlinked before return
rtaioblocking|salivo_aio_blocking|int|int,int|runs on the bounded blocking pool; suspends the task|any thread|result via rtaiolastvalue
rtaiochannew|salivo_aio_chan_new|int|int|never|any thread|caller owns the channel handle; capacity 0 means unbounded
rtaiochansend|salivo_aio_chan_send|int|int,int|suspends while a bounded channel is full|any thread|borrows the handle
rtaiochantrysend|salivo_aio_chan_try_send|int|int,int|never|any thread|borrows the handle
rtaiochanrecv|salivo_aio_chan_recv|int|int|suspends while the channel is empty|any thread|value via rtaiolastvalue
rtaiochantryrecv|salivo_aio_chan_try_recv|int|int|never|any thread|value via rtaiolastvalue
rtaiochanclose|salivo_aio_chan_close|int|int|never|any thread|closes for sending; buffered values stay receivable
rtaiochanlen|salivo_aio_chan_len|int|int|never|any thread|borrows the handle
rtaiochannewtext|salivo_aio_chan_new_text|int|int|never|any thread|caller owns the text channel handle; the channel owns buffered strings (copies)
rtaiochansendtext|salivo_aio_chan_send_text|int|int,string|suspends while a bounded channel is full|any thread|copies the text; an undelivered copy is freed
rtaiochantrysendtext|salivo_aio_chan_try_send_text|int|int,string|never|any thread|copies the text; an undelivered copy is freed
rtaiochanrecvtext|salivo_aio_chan_recv_text|int|int|suspends while the channel is empty|any thread|received text via rtaiolasttext
rtaiochantryrecvtext|salivo_aio_chan_try_recv_text|int|int|never|any thread|received text via rtaiolasttext
rtaiotcplisten|salivo_aio_tcp_listen|int|string,int,int|never (numeric hosts); name lookup runs on the blocking pool|any thread|caller owns the listener handle
rtaiotcpaccept|salivo_aio_tcp_accept|int|int|suspends until a connection arrives|any thread|caller owns the returned stream handle
rtaiotcpconnect|salivo_aio_tcp_connect|int|string,int|suspends until connected|any thread|caller owns the returned stream handle
rtaioread|salivo_aio_read|int|int,int,int|suspends until data, EOF or error|one reader per handle at a time|reads at most cap bytes into caller-owned memory
rtaiowrite|salivo_aio_write|int|int,int,int|suspends until every byte is written|one writer per handle at a time|writes len bytes from caller-owned memory
rtaiowritetext|salivo_aio_write_text|int|int,string|suspends until every byte is written|one writer per handle at a time|writes the UTF-8 bytes of text (without the NUL)
rtaiotcpshutdown|salivo_aio_tcp_shutdown|int|int|never|any thread|half-closes the sending direction
rtaioclose|salivo_aio_close|int|int|never for sockets; file close runs on the blocking pool|any thread|consumes the handle; a second close returns InvalidHandle
rtaiolocalport|salivo_aio_local_port|int|int|never|any thread|borrows the handle
rtaioudpbind|salivo_aio_udp_bind|int|string,int|never|any thread|caller owns the socket handle
rtaioudpsendto|salivo_aio_udp_send_to|int|int,int,int,string,int|suspends until the datagram is queued|any thread|reads len bytes from caller-owned memory
rtaioudprecvfrom|salivo_aio_udp_recv_from|int|int,int,int|suspends until a datagram arrives|any thread|peer endpoint (ipv4 * 65536 + port) via rtaiolastvalue
rtaiofileopen|salivo_aio_file_open|int|string,int|runs on the blocking pool; suspends the task|any thread|caller owns the file handle
rtaiofileseek|salivo_aio_file_seek|int|int,int,int|never|one user per handle at a time|borrows the handle
rtaioflush|salivo_aio_flush|int|int|runs on the blocking pool; suspends the task|any thread|borrows the handle
rtaiobufnew|salivo_aio_buf_new|int|int|never|any thread|caller owns the buffer; free with rtaiobuffree
rtaiobuffree|salivo_aio_buf_free|int|int|never|any thread|consumes the buffer
rtaiobufget|salivo_aio_buf_get|int|int,int|never|any thread|borrows the buffer
rtaiobufset|salivo_aio_buf_set|int|int,int,int|never|any thread|borrows the buffer
rtaiobufputtext|salivo_aio_buf_put_text|int|int,int,string|never|any thread|copies at most cap bytes of text into the buffer
rtaiobufstr|salivo_aio_buf_str|string|int,int|never|any thread|returns a new heap string owned by the caller
rtaioargnew|salivo_aio_arg_new|int|int|never|any thread|argument block for an async func call (compiler-generated); freed by rtaioargfree
rtaioargsetint|salivo_aio_arg_set_int|int|int,int,int|never|single owner|stores an int (or bool) argument
rtaioargsettext|salivo_aio_arg_set_text|int|int,int,string|never|single owner|stores a copy of a string argument
rtaioargint|salivo_aio_arg_int|int|int,int|never|single owner|reads an int argument
rtaioargstr|salivo_aio_arg_get_str|string|int,int|never|single owner|hands the copied string argument to the caller
rtaioargfree|salivo_aio_arg_free|int|int|never|single owner|frees the block and any strings not handed out
rtaioerrorname|salivo_aio_error_name_str|string|int|never|any thread|returns a static string
# ---- Stage 36.2 HTTP/1.1 + HTTP/2 (salivo_aio_http.inc). Connections and exchanges are handles in the
# runtime's table; an exchange refers to its connection by handle only (no ownership cycle).
rtaiohttpserver|salivo_aio_http_server|int|int,int|never|any thread|takes ownership of the TCP stream (the connection closes it); proto 0 auto, 1 HTTP/1.1, 2 HTTP/2 prior knowledge; caller owns the connection handle; errors: InvalidArgument, InvalidHandle, Refused (connection limit), Os; platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttpclient|salivo_aio_http_client|int|int,int|never|any thread|takes ownership of the TCP stream; proto 1 or 2; caller owns the connection handle; errors: InvalidArgument, InvalidHandle, Refused (connection limit), Os; platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttpset|salivo_aio_http_set|int|int,int,int|never|any thread; before the connection starts|sets limit `key` of a connection (0 = process defaults; key 100 = maximum connections); errors: InvalidArgument (key/value, or a buffer/SETTINGS key after HTTP/2 started), InvalidHandle; platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttpnext|salivo_aio_http_next|int|int|suspends until a request head is parsed|one acceptor per connection|caller owns the returned exchange handle; Eof when the connection ends; errors: Eof (connection ended); BadMessage, InvalidHeader, InvalidFraming, HeaderTooLarge, BodyTooLarge, VersionNotSupported (request rejected with 4xx/5xx); ProtocolError, Compression, FlowControl (HTTP/2 connection error); Timeout, Cancelled, Closed; InvalidArgument (response pending, second acceptor); platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttprequest|salivo_aio_http_request|int|int,string,string|never|any thread|copies method and target; caller owns the exchange handle; errors: InvalidArgument (syntax, exchange in progress), Closed, InvalidHandle; platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttpaddheader|salivo_aio_http_add_header|int|int,string,string|never|exchange owner|validates and copies an outbound field; rejects CR/LF/NUL and framing fields; errors: InvalidArgument (syntax, CR/LF/NUL, framing field, head already sent), HeaderTooLarge; platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttpsend|salivo_aio_http_send|int|int,int,int|suspends until the head is written (HTTP/2 client: until a stream slot is free)|exchange owner|status (0 on a client) and body length (-1 streams); errors: InvalidArgument, GoingAway, StreamReset, Timeout, Cancelled, Closed; platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttpwrite|salivo_aio_http_write|int|int,int,int|suspends until written (socket and flow-control backpressure)|exchange owner|writes len bytes of caller-owned memory; bodies above 4 KiB go to the socket without a copy; errors: InvalidArgument (head not sent, beyond the declared length), StreamReset, Timeout, Cancelled, Closed; platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttpwritetext|salivo_aio_http_write_text|int|int,string|suspends until written|exchange owner|writes the UTF-8 bytes of text; errors: InvalidArgument, StreamReset, Timeout, Cancelled, Closed; platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttpfinish|salivo_aio_http_finish|int|int|suspends until the terminator is written|exchange owner|ends the outbound body; a short fixed-length body fails and aborts the message; errors: InvalidFraming (short fixed-length body), StreamReset, Timeout, Cancelled, Closed; platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttpresponse|salivo_aio_http_response|int|int|suspends until the response head arrives|exchange owner|returns the status code; errors: InvalidArgument, StreamReset, Refused, GoingAway, BadMessage, InvalidFraming, ProtocolError, Timeout, Cancelled, Closed; platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttpread|salivo_aio_http_read|int|int,int,int|suspends until body bytes arrive|exchange owner|copies at most cap body bytes into caller memory; Eof at the end of the body; errors: Eof (end of body), BodyTooLarge, InvalidFraming, InvalidHeader (trailer), StreamReset, Timeout, Cancelled, Closed; platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttpnextchunk|salivo_aio_http_next_chunk|int|int|suspends until body bytes arrive|exchange owner|makes the next body piece the exchange's current view (no copy) and returns its length; the view lives until the next call or free; errors: Eof (end of body), BodyTooLarge, InvalidFraming, InvalidHeader (trailer), StreamReset, Timeout, Cancelled, Closed; platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttpchunkbyte|salivo_aio_http_chunk_byte|int|int,int|never|exchange owner|byte i of the current view; errors: InvalidArgument (index outside the view), InvalidHandle; platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttptext|salivo_aio_http_text_str|string|int,int|never|exchange owner|0 method, 1 target, 2 path, 3 query, 4 authority, 5 scheme, 6 reason, 7 protocol; new string owned by the caller; errors: none ("" for an unknown key or handle); platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttpheader|salivo_aio_http_header_str|string|int,string,int|never|exchange owner|n-th value of an inbound field (case-insensitive name); new string owned by the caller; errors: none ("" when absent); platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttpheadercount|salivo_aio_http_header_count|int|int,string|never|exchange owner|number of inbound fields with the name ("" counts all); errors: InvalidHandle; platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttpheaderat|salivo_aio_http_header_at_str|string|int,int,int|never|exchange owner|name (part 0) or value (part 1) of inbound field i; new string owned by the caller; errors: none ("" outside the field list); platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttptrailer|salivo_aio_http_trailer_str|string|int,string|never|exchange owner|inbound trailer value after the body ended; new string owned by the caller; errors: none ("" when absent or before the body ended); platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttpinfo|salivo_aio_http_info|int|int,int|never|any thread|integer facts about an exchange or connection (docs/STAGE_36_2_HTTP.md); errors: InvalidArgument (key), InvalidHandle; platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttpreset|salivo_aio_http_reset|int|int,int|never (queues RST_STREAM)|any thread|HTTP/2 resets the stream with the code; HTTP/1.1 closes the connection; errors: InvalidArgument (code), InvalidHandle; platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttpfree|salivo_aio_http_free|int|int|never|any thread|consumes the exchange handle; an unfinished HTTP/2 stream is reset, an unfinished HTTP/1.1 message closes the connection; errors: InvalidHandle; platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttpgoaway|salivo_aio_http_goaway|int|int,int|never (queues GOAWAY)|any thread|graceful shutdown: no new streams; next() returns Eof once queued requests are taken; errors: InvalidArgument (code), InvalidHandle; platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttpping|salivo_aio_http_ping|int|int|suspends until the PING ACK|any thread|returns the round trip in microseconds (HTTP/2 only); errors: Unsupported (HTTP/1.1), InvalidArgument (PING outstanding), Full, Timeout, Cancelled, Closed; platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttpclose|salivo_aio_http_close|int|int|never|any thread|consumes the connection handle and closes the socket; waiting exchanges fail with Closed; errors: InvalidHandle; platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttpauthority|salivo_aio_http_authority|int|int,string|never|any thread|copies the default Host / :authority of a client connection; errors: InvalidArgument (server connection, invalid text), InvalidHandle; platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiohttpstat|salivo_aio_http_stat|int|int|never|any thread|process-wide HTTP counters (copies, pool, live objects); errors: InvalidArgument (key); platform: identical on every 36.1 backend (no platform code)
rtaiocall|salivo_aio_call|int|int,int|whatever the called function does|any thread|synchronous call of a Salivo func(int) -> int value (Stage 36.3 handlers and middleware); errors: InvalidArgument (null function); platform: identical everywhere (no platform code)
rtaiohttppeer|salivo_aio_http_peer_str|string|int|never|any thread|textual IP address of the peer of an exchange or connection; new string owned by the caller; errors: none ("" when unknown); platform: getpeername on every 36.1 backend
